summary: Fuzz keylime's IMA measurement-list line parser (keylime#1139)
description: |
    Fuzzer test for keylime/ima/ast.py, the parser that consumes individual
    IMA measurement-list lines originating from a potentially compromised
    agent, a Tier-1 fuzzing target identified in keylime/keylime#1139:

      * ast.Entry(line)                  - full measurement-list line parser
      * ast.Digest(field, legacy)        - "<hex>" / "<alg>:<hash>" parser
      * ast.Name(field, legacy)          - path/name, incl. legacy fixed-length
      * ast.Signature(hexdata)           - binary "ima-sig" signature header

    The verifier drives Entry() in keylime/ima/ima.py _process_measurement_list
    inside a loop that only catches ast.ParserError. The parser's contract is
    therefore to reject any malformed line with a ParserError and nothing else;
    any OTHER exception type escaping it (ValueError, struct.error,
    UnicodeEncodeError, ...) is not caught by the verifier loop and crashes the
    whole quote-verification pipeline - a remote DoS. The test hunts for
    exactly that class of non-ParserError escape (e.g. the legacy "n" name path
    computing TCG_EVENT_NAME_LEN_MAX - len(name_bytes) and raising on an
    over-long name), plus hangs and resource exhaustion.

    The test runs in two layers. A deterministic replayer feeds a generated
    corpus of valid and known-adversarial lines/fields through each parser
    under a wall-clock timeout and requires every input to be either parsed or
    rejected with ParserError; this needs only the installed keylime package
    and runs on every platform. When atheris (coverage-guided, libFuzzer-
    backed) can be imported or pip-installed, a bounded coverage-guided
    campaign is run on top, seeded from the same corpus; any reproducer atheris
    saves fails the test and is attached to the results.

    Campaign budgets can be raised for longer local runs via the
    FUZZ_MAX_TOTAL_TIME, FUZZ_TIMEOUT and FUZZ_RSS_MB environment variables.
contact: Karel Srot <ksrot@redhat.com>
component:
  - keylime
test: ./test.sh
framework: beakerlib
tag:
